      "component_id": "ED26-P15-CH-finite-probability-C010",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "Event independence (pairwise and mutual, FP 220-229) and conditional independence (FP 236-238) are supplied, but random-variable independence is defined only for two variables X,Y (FP 231-235). The held source's Definition 4.4 (Grinstead-Snell sec. 4.1, p. 142) defines mutual independence of n random variables X1,...,Xn by factorization of P(X1=r1,...,Xn=rn), with the joint random variable of Definition 4.3; no n-variable mutual independence of finite random variables appears in this entry or elsewhere in the chapter. The source's Definition 4.2 variant (mutual independence of n events equivalently stated for every choice of each A_j or its complement, p. 141) and its remark that the single full-product identity does not imply mutual independence are also not stated; the complement criterion at FP 246-247 / FA 160-170 covers only a pair. The entry therefore does not preserve the identified source variant for random-variable independence.",
